From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: reader network configuration, clocks and reader state

Stubs (E_NOTIMPL / FIXME), as documented now. The reader has no network
source, so the network settings are kept for the program to read back, with
the Windows Media Format SDK's conventions for the rest.

- IWMReaderNetworkConfig / IWMReaderNetworkConfig2: buffering time (default
  5 s), the UDP port ranges (two-call array getter, ASF_E_BUFFERTOOSMALL),
  per-protocol proxy settings for http, mms and rtsp (setting 0..3, host
  name, port, exception list, bypass for local; the protocols are also what
  GetNumProtocolsSupported / GetSupportedProtocolName list),
  EnableMulticast/HTTP/UDP/TCP, content caching, fast cache, resends,
  thinning, forced proxy re-detection, connection bandwidth, accelerated
  streaming duration, auto reconnect limit, max packet size, the logging URL
  list. String getters answer a NULL buffer with the length including the
  terminator and a short one with ASF_E_BUFFERTOOSMALL and the length;
  NULL pointers and unknown protocols are E_INVALIDARG.
- IWMReaderAdvanced: Get/SetUserProvidedClock (the getter was E_NOTIMPL),
  Get/SetManualStreamSelection, Get/SetReceiveSelectionCallbacks,
  Get/SetLogClientID, Get/SetPlayMode (0..3), GetReceiveStreamSamples,
  GetStatistics (zero counters, cbSize checked), SetClientInfo,
  NotifyLateDelivery, AddLogParam / SendLogParams.
- IReferenceClock on the reader: GetTime (S_FALSE when it did not advance),
  AdviseTime and AdvisePeriodic (timer queue timers that set the event or
  release the semaphore, a time in the past signals at once, E_INVALIDARG for
  a bad period), Unadvise (S_FALSE for an unknown cookie).
- IWMReaderStreamClock: GetTime (the delivered time with the program's clock,
  the time since Start otherwise), SetTimer / KillTimer on an open reader:
  IWMReaderCallbackAdvanced::OnTime is called with the timer's parameter when
  the stream time reaches it (DeliverTime moves it when the program provides
  the clock); the timers go away with Close.
- QueryInterface of an unsupported interface is a WARN, not a FIXME.

